IMPORT prelude

-- Oaths and Declarations Act 2000 (Singapore) -- who must swear, and the alternatives of affirmation and caution (ss 4-6, 8);
-- before whom a statutory declaration must be made in and outside Singapore (ss 11, 12); the offence of a false statutory
-- declaration (s 14); and oaths of office and judicial oaths, including taking them by live video link (ss 15, 16).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ODA2000.txt, version in
-- force from 1 December 2023, with the amendment by Act 25 of 2023 (s 15(2A), wef 01/12/2023) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. The Act is short; this row takes the
-- provisions with decision content. Not encoded: the power to administer oaths (s 3), the form and manner of oaths left to the
-- Rules of Court (s 7), voluntary declarations and declarations required by other written law beyond their pointer to ss 11-12
-- (ss 9, 10), proof of execution of a will by declaration (s 13), regulations and amendment of Schedules (ss 17, 18), savings
-- (s 19), and the text of the Schedule forms beyond the wording s 16 changes. Who is a "prescribed person" under s 11(1)(b) is
-- left to regulations, which were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Oaths and Declarations Act 2000`

§§ `4 -- who must take an oath`

-- s 4(1): "oaths must be taken by" (a) "a person who may be lawfully examined, or who may give or be required to give
-- evidence, by or before a court or person acting judicially"; (b) "an interpreter of questions put to, and of evidence given
-- by", such a person.
-- s 4(2): not (a) "the official interpreter of a court" or (b) "a certificated interpreter in the public service", "when
-- performing his or her duties as such interpreter, if he or she has taken an oath to faithfully discharge those duties".
-- s 2: "person acting judicially" means "a person, tribunal, commission, committee or other body having by law or consent of
-- the parties power to receive evidence".
GIVEN `gives evidence before a court or person acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `interprets for such a witness` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an official court interpreter or certificated public-service interpreter on duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has taken an oath to discharge interpreter duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an oath must be taken` IF
        (`gives evidence before a court or person acting judicially` OR `interprets for such a witness`)
    AND NOT (`is an official court interpreter or certificated public-service interpreter on duty`
             AND `has taken an oath to discharge interpreter duties`)

§§ `5, 6 -- affirmation and caution in lieu of oath`

-- s 5: a person required to take an oath who "(a) is a Hindu or Muslim or of some other religion according to which oaths
-- are not of binding force; or (b) has a conscientious objection to taking an oath" "may, instead of taking an oath, make an
-- affirmation".
-- s 6: where the person "ought not, in the opinion of the court or person acting judicially, to take an oath or make an
-- affirmation by reason of immaturity of age", the person "may ... be cautioned ... to state the truth, the whole truth, and
-- nothing but the truth".
--
-- INFERENCE: s 6 says the immature person "ought not" to swear or affirm; this encoding reads that as excluding oath and
-- affirmation once the court has formed that opinion. The text says "may ... be cautioned", not "must".
DECLARE Undertaking IS ONE OF
    `an oath`
    `an affirmation`
    `a caution`

GIVEN `the undertaking` IS AN Undertaking,
      `religion holds oaths not binding` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `conscientiously objects to oaths` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `court thinks the witness too young to swear or affirm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the witness may give the undertaking` IF
    CONSIDER `the undertaking`
    WHEN `an oath` THEN NOT `court thinks the witness too young to swear or affirm`
    WHEN `an affirmation` THEN
            (`religion holds oaths not binding` OR `conscientiously objects to oaths`)
        AND (NOT `court thinks the witness too young to swear or affirm`)
    WHEN `a caution` THEN `court thinks the witness too young to swear or affirm`

§§ `8 -- omissions and irregularities`

-- s 8: "No omission to take an oath, make an affirmation or administer a caution, and no irregularity in the form or manner"
-- may "(a) invalidate any proceedings or render inadmissible any evidence ...; or (b) affect any obligation of the person ...
-- to state the truth."
DECLARE Defect IS ONE OF
    `no oath taken`
    `no affirmation made`
    `no caution administered`
    `an oath in the wrong form`
    `a caution in the wrong manner`
    `no defect`

GIVEN `the defect` IS A Defect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defect makes the evidence inadmissible` IF FALSE

GIVEN `the defect` IS A Defect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the witness is still obliged to tell the truth` IF TRUE

§§ `11, 12 -- before whom a statutory declaration is made`

-- s 11(1): a statutory declaration made in Singapore "(a) must be in the form set out in the First Schedule; and (b) must be
-- made before a court, a person acting judicially, or a prescribed person". (2): other written law conferring power to take
-- declarations is not affected (not encoded).
-- s 12(1): one made "in the United Kingdom or any part of the Commonwealth other than Singapore must be made before a notary
-- public or justice of the peace of that country, or other person having authority under any law ... in that country".
-- (2): one made "in any place that is not part of the Commonwealth must be made before a consul or vice consul or before any
-- person having authority under any law ... in that place".
--
-- Read as written: s 12 does not require the First Schedule form; a notary public is not named for a non-Commonwealth place,
-- and a consul is not named for a Commonwealth place -- each qualifies there only if local law gives that person authority.
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `Singapore`
    `the United Kingdom or another Commonwealth country`
    `a place outside the Commonwealth`

DECLARE Taker IS ONE OF
    `a court`
    `a person acting judicially`
    `a prescribed person`
    `a local notary public`
    `a local justice of the peace`
    `a person authorised by local law to take declarations`
    `a consul or vice consul`
    `a friend of the declarant`

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `the taker` IS A Taker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the taker may receive the declaration` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `Singapore` THEN
        CONSIDER `the taker`
        WHEN `a court` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person acting judicially` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a prescribed person` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `the United Kingdom or another Commonwealth country` THEN
        CONSIDER `the taker`
        WHEN `a local notary public` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a local justice of the peace` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person authorised by local law to take declarations` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `a place outside the Commonwealth` THEN
        CONSIDER `the taker`
        WHEN `a consul or vice consul` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person authorised by local law to take declarations` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the First Schedule form is required` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `Singapore` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `the taker` IS A Taker, `uses the First Schedule form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaration is made in the manner the Act provides` IF
        `the taker may receive the declaration` `the place` `the taker`
    AND ((NOT `the First Schedule form is required` `the place`) OR `uses the First Schedule form`)

§§ `14 -- false statutory declarations`

-- s 14(1): an offence where a person "(a) makes in a statutory declaration a statement which is false, and which the person
-- knows or has reason to believe is false or does not believe to be true, touching any point material to the object for which
-- the declaration is made or used; or (b) corruptly uses or attempts to use as true any statutory declaration made in or
-- outside Singapore knowing the declaration to be false in any material point".
-- s 14(3): "(1)(a) applies to the making of a statutory declaration outside Singapore if the person knows or has reason to
-- believe that the statutory declaration is intended to be used in Singapore".
-- INFERENCE: a declaration made outside Singapore without that knowledge falls outside (1)(a); the text does not say so in
-- terms, but (3) would otherwise do nothing.
-- s 14(4): "No prosecution may be instituted under this section without the written consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `made a false statement in a statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or believed it false, or did not believe it true` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the statement was on a material point` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made the declaration outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reason to believe it was for use in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `corruptly used a declaration known false in a material point` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a false declaration offence is committed` IF
        (    `made a false statement in a statutory declaration`
         AND `knew or believed it false, or did not believe it true`
         AND `the statement was on a material point`
         AND ((NOT `made the declaration outside Singapore`) OR `knew or had reason to believe it was for use in Singapore`))
    OR `corruptly used a declaration known false in a material point`

GIVEN `has the Public Prosecutor's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may be instituted` IF `has the Public Prosecutor's written consent`

-- s 14(1)(c): if made or used "in any stage of a judicial proceeding", imprisonment "which may extend to 7 years" and "also
-- liable to a fine"; (d) "in any other case", imprisonment "which may extend to 3 years" and also liable to a fine.
-- s 14(2): "(a) a trial before a subordinate military court within the meaning of the Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972 is a
-- judicial proceeding"; (b) a stage of a judicial proceeding includes "(i) an investigation directed by law that is preliminary
-- to a proceeding before a court" and "(ii) an investigation directed by a court, and conducted under the authority of a court".
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `a court trial`
    `a subordinate military court trial`
    `an investigation directed by law preliminary to court proceedings`
    `an investigation directed by a court`
    `an application to a government agency`
    `a private transaction`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is a stage of a judicial proceeding` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `an application to a government agency` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private transaction` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    IF `the use is a stage of a judicial proceeding` `the use` THEN 7 ELSE 3

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fine may also be imposed` IF TRUE

§§ `15, 16 -- oaths of office and judicial oaths`

-- s 15(1): the oath of allegiance (Second Schedule Part 1) and the oath of office (Part 2) "must be tendered to and taken by
-- all persons required under any written law to take an oath of office". (2): the oath of allegiance and the judicial oath
-- (Part 3) for "all persons required under any written law to take a judicial oath".
DECLARE OathRequirement IS ONE OF
    `an oath of office`
    `a judicial oath`

DECLARE ScheduleOath IS ONE OF
    `the oath of allegiance`
    `the oath of office`
    `the judicial oath`

GIVEN `the requirement` IS AN OathRequirement, `the oath` IS A ScheduleOath
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the oath must be taken` IF
    CONSIDER `the oath`
    WHEN `the oath of allegiance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the oath of office` THEN
        CONSIDER `the requirement`
        WHEN `an oath of office` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `the judicial oath` THEN
        CONSIDER `the requirement`
        WHEN `a judicial oath` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 16: on the same two grounds as s 5, a person required to take an oath of office or judicial oath "may ... make an
-- affirmation in the form of those oaths, substituting the words 'solemnly, sincerely and truly declare and affirm' for the
-- word 'swear' and omitting the words 'So help me God'".
GIVEN `religion holds oaths not binding` IS A BOOLEAN, `conscientiously objects to oaths` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office holder may affirm instead` IF
    `religion holds oaths not binding` OR `conscientiously objects to oaths`

GIVEN `is affirming` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the words So help me God are said` IF NOT `is affirming`

-- s 15(2A) (Act 25 of 2023 wef 01/12/2023): "To avoid doubt", an oath under (1) or (2), or an affirmation under s 16, may be
-- taken "through a live video link or live television link" that allows the person administering it to "(a) maintain visual
-- contact and communicate with the person ... and any interpreter present, throughout the process; (b) confirm the identity of
-- the person ... and any interpreter present; and (c) if the oath or affirmation is to be subscribed, verify by inspection the
-- oath or affirmation to be subscribed".
-- Read as written, (2A) attaches only to oaths of office and judicial oaths. Nothing in this Act's text extends it to a
-- witness's oath under s 4 or a statutory declaration under s 11.
DECLARE Occasion IS ONE OF
    `an office or judicial oath under s 15`
    `a witness oath under s 4`
    `a statutory declaration under s 11`

GIVEN `the occasion` IS AN Occasion,
      `link keeps visual contact and communication throughout` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `link lets identity be confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the oath is to be subscribed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `link lets the subscribed oath be inspected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act provides for taking it by video link` IF
        (CONSIDER `the occasion`
         WHEN `an office or judicial oath under s 15` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `link keeps visual contact and communication throughout`
    AND `link lets identity be confirmed`
    AND ((NOT `the oath is to be subscribed`) OR `link lets the subscribed oath be inspected`)
